From ebcc35f44458448d66e51267926646da746ec401 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:13:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] settings: the help of the two settings of VRR says what they
 do now

The help of "Video at its own rate with VRR" said that it takes SDR and
HDR10 only, and that on NVIDIA "HDMI variable refresh rate (VRR)" must be
on; the help of that setting said that, off, Kodi asks the driver to leave
VRR off in every change of mode. They now say:
- HDR10+ goes at its own rate with VRR where the graphics driver sends it
  next to the VRR packet (NV_HDR10PLUS_WITH_VRR: the RTX 40 and RTX 50
  series), and changes the mode elsewhere;
- the setting turns HDMI VRR on by itself (CHdmiVrrOff::Allowed() takes
  either setting: the other one never had to be on);
- on a display that declares VRR and has no mode at the rate of films at
  the resolution of the menus, a video goes at its own rate with VRR also
  with the setting off, and the modes of its menus leave VRR on
  (VRR_VIDEO::AutoForDisplay()).
In English and in the three Spanish languages; only the texts change.
